e>375</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12019016</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b19-ehp-116-1411"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zeiger</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Beaty</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Is there a relationship between risk factors for oral clefts?</article-title><source>Teratology</source><volume>66</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>205</fpage><lpage>208</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12397627</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20-ehp-116-1411"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zeiger</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Beaty</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Liang</surname><given-names>KY</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Oral clefts, maternal smoking, and TGFA: a meta-analysis of gene-environment interaction</article-title><source>Cleft Palate Craniofac J</source><volume>42</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>58</fpage><lpage>63</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15643916</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="f1-ehp-116-1411" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Geographic locations of 72 air pollution monitoring stations (shown in dots) in Taiwan. Shaded area indicates the mountain area that has no air monitoring stations.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ehp-116-1411f1"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-ehp-116-1411" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Characteristics of controls and cases of cleft lip in Taiwan, 2001&#x02013;2003 [no. (%)].</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Characteristic</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Controls</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cases</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Total<